  "summary": "Valley National Bancorp's $340m acquisition of fintech Bluevine triggered modest negative sentiment for small regional banks (e.g., Coastal Financial), reflecting consolidation/competition in small-business digital banking. Short-term transmission is competitive pressure on deposits/SMB lending and fee income for smaller banks, so financials (regional banks) are likely modestly hurt over the next few trading days. Market relevance is low-to-moderate given the small deal size and limited direct impact on major tracked banks or other sectors.",
